t3v (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New incremental search kernel, now the default (--algo incremental):
    enumerates candidates by repeated basepoint addition with batched modular
    inversion instead of hashing a fresh seed per candidate. Measured 218x
    faster than the original kernel on an RTX 4070. The original path remains
    available as --algo seed.
  * New CLI: --bonus for prefixes saved if found but which never keep the run
    alive, --count to collect several matches per prefix, and --algo to pick
    the kernel. The run now exits with a summary once the required prefixes
    are found instead of looping forever. Added --version.
  * Live per-GPU dashboard with per-prefix statistics, and plain status lines
    when output is not a terminal.
  * Fixed a matcher bug where prefixes whose length is a multiple of 8 never
    matched.
  * Prefixes are normalized to lowercase and validated up front. Previously an
    uppercase prefix caused every genuine match to be discarded forever, and an
    invalid base32 character produced two unrelated panics.
  * Key files are now created mode 0600 rather than inheriting the umask, are
    never silently overwritten, and are fsynced before being reported.
  * Keys saved from a single GPU launch were algebraically related, so
    compromise of one exposed the others. At most one match per launch is now
    kept and the run re-seeds before continuing.
  * Concurrent matches no longer race on a shared output slot; each prefix has
    a ring of slots claimed with an atomic increment.
  * Progress reporting replaced with P(found) and a constant expected time to
    the next hit, which is what a memoryless search actually offers.
  * Ship a man page, copyright file and this changelog; declare library
    dependencies; strip the shipped binary.

 -- Server Man <dupastiy@proton.me>  Sun, 09 Aug 2026 20:50:00 +0000

